nt :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{-3}^{3}{x}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423208} {:answer/id #uuid "5af7a6f0-0077-5043-a558-dd52db115cb0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{-3}^{3}{x}^{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\pi x)\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423212} {:answer/id #uuid "736d59ea-f33a-5ef5-b1fc-b2bef5e99802" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }{x}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423218} {:answer/id #uuid "b13038c9-0e29-5c99-ae13-0cda1eb89b60" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }{x}^{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423228} {:answer/id #uuid "c8e1fc56-3d17-5a34-80f2-d7006b2e8f19" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{-3}^{3}{x}^{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\pi x)\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423231}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c8e1fc56-3d17-5a34-80f2-d7006b2e8f19" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{-3}^{3}{x}^{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\pi x)\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423231} :answer-field/id #uuid "c2939d33-2683-5e5e-b87f-2f0d344063b9" :answer-field/key "field-5" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423250} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "00561c08-ad3b-5d9b-ac8d-d1c849b75bfa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\pi }{\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }f(x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{6L}{\\pi }x)\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423194} {:answer/id #uuid "2e50c090-e2ce-5c63-a2c9-146ede30820c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{L}{\\int }_{-L}^{L}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423200} {:answer/id #uuid "541c2cbf-9b2c-5091-88fa-4b3a5ac3c8c0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{L}{\\int }_{-L}^{L}f(x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{6\\pi }{L}x)\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423210} {:answer/id #uuid "6b54c63d-6367-5121-8b46-fa32b2d6365f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{L}{\\int }_{-L}^{L}f(x)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{6\\pi }{L}x)\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423214} {:answer/id #uuid "73ee4e81-95a1-562c-b139-d8c63a070d9c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\pi }{\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }f(x)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{6L}{\\pi }x)\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423219} {:answer/id #uuid "e2f12b06-46ca-594c-ba89-e1d7d2ac11d1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\pi }{\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }f(x)\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423236}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6b54c63d-6367-5121-8b46-fa32b2d6365f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{L}{\\int }_{-L}^{L}f(x)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{6\\pi }{L}x)\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423214} :answer-field/id #uuid "d24575e5-699f-5456-96dd-cc5375bcde7a" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423252}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "4886c497-1cb0-54c5-b33a-8a4433090897" :question/math-academy-id "q-341778" :question/problem "Let $f(x)$ be the $2L$-periodic extension of a function $F(x)$ from $x\\in [-L,L)$ to $x\\in R.$\nSelect the correct options in the reasoning below.\n\nThe Fourier series of $f$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x)∼\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡({{field-1}})+{b}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡({{field-2}}).\n$$\n\nThe $6$th sine coefficient of the series is\n\n$$\n{b}_{6}={{field-3}}.\n$$\n\nGiven that $F(x)={x}^{3}$ and $L=3,$ the $6$th sine coefficient becomes\n\n$$\n{b}_{6}={{field-4}}\\,\\cdot \\,{{field-5}}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that multiplying the argument of a function by $k\\ne 0$ represents the horizontal stretching of the corresponding graph by a factor of $\\frac{1}{k}.$\n\nNow, let $s=\\frac{\\pi }{L}x.$ Then, since $f(x)$ has a period of $2L,$ the function\n\n$$\ng(s)=f(\\frac{L}{\\pi }s)\n$$\n\nmust have a period of $2L\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{L}=2\\pi .$ \n\nThe Fourier series of $g(s)$ is\n\n$$\ng(s)∼\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(ns)+{b}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(ns),\n$$\n\nwhere:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{0} & =\\frac{1}{\\pi }{\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }g(s)\\,\\text{d}s \\\\ {a}_{n} & =\\frac{1}{\\pi }{\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }g(s)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(ns)\\,\\text{d}s,\\,n\\ge 1 \\\\ {b}_{n} & =\\frac{1}{\\pi }{\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }g(s)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(ns)\\,\\text{d}s,\\,n\\ge 1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $s=\\frac{\\pi }{L}x$ and using the fact that $g(s)=f(\\frac{L}{\\pi }s),$ we get the Fourier series of $f(x):$\n\n$$\nf(x)∼\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi }{L}x)+{b}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi }{L}x)\n$$\n\nTherefore, $6$th sine coefficient of $f(x)$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{b}_{6} & =\\frac{1}{\\pi }{\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }g(s)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(6s)\\,\\text{d}s \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\pi }{\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }f(\\frac{L}{\\pi }s)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(6s)\\,\\text{d}s \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\pi }{\\int }_{-L}^{L}f(\\frac{L}{\\pi }\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{L}x)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(6\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{L}x)\\,\\text{d}(\\frac{\\pi }{L}x) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\pi }\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{L}{\\int }_{-L}^{L}f(x)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{6\\pi }{L}x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{L}{\\int }_{-L}^{L}f(x)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{6\\pi }{L}x)\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting $L=3$ and $f(x)={x}^{3},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{b}_{6} & =\\frac{1}{3}{\\int }_{-3}^{3}{x}^{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{6\\pi }{3}x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot {\\int }_{-3}^{3}{x}^{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\pi x)\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186423255 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186221443 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "12ff3452-19b6-566a-8b39-ad880dee8858" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Effects of the Horizontal Scaling on Coefficients"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "330555a3-3265-5f64-bc94-45b597110cad" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{n}{L\\pi }x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423203} {:answer/id #uuid "4e94721c-9801-5a97-a7fe-871db3f9b6da" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{n\\pi }{L}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423209} {:answer/id #uuid "8c7489e7-133a-5140-a832-5843b22b1762" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{nL}{\\pi }x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423224} {:answer/id #uuid "f65d51dd-ac13-5c57-b660-bc0774154b5a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{L}{n\\pi }x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423241}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4e94721c-9801-5a97-a7fe-871db3f9b6da" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{n\\pi }{L}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423209} :answer-field/id #uuid "20188161-12bf-54c3-b2b9-4680bbcd0ad2" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select}