swer/value "\\frac{4}{\\pi }" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423227}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "282319fc-9f02-5762-9c82-02e738760f50" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423198} :answer-field/id #uuid "973bb348-68db-5f8b-b078-a1a0c39d3c7a" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423248} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "477216e7-29ff-535c-919b-7c0025478625" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{-4}^{4}{cos}^{2}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423207} {:answer/id #uuid "9e7c78ab-810e-5194-923c-bb29e87bc1a4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }{cos}^{3}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423226} {:answer/id #uuid "d1a2e1c1-74f1-595f-8870-09a1c08cfd5d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423233} {:answer/id #uuid "e582708c-30ab-51b7-8fac-ed5cfb399655" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{-4}^{4}{cos}^{2}⁡(x)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi x)\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423237} {:answer/id #uuid "e671311a-a6c6-5590-aa9c-c58e95336c2b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{-4}^{4}{cos}^{2}⁡(x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi x)\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423238} {:answer/id #uuid "ff0d9dcc-3414-5481-a1ea-2423a23ed503" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }{cos}^{2}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423242}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "477216e7-29ff-535c-919b-7c0025478625" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{-4}^{4}{cos}^{2}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423207} :answer-field/id #uuid "e5dac63d-6b9e-5dfb-b42e-18dabc9a7e34" :answer-field/key "field-5" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423253}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d180264d-6aaf-5aca-a8a3-12aea15eb407" :question/math-academy-id "q-341785" :question/problem "Let $f(x)$ be the $2L$-periodic extension of a function $F(x)$ from $x\\in [-L,L)$ to $x\\in R.$\nSelect the correct options in the reasoning below.\n\nThe Fourier series of $f$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x)∼\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡({{field-1}})+{b}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡({{field-2}}).\n$$\n\nThe constant coefficient of the series is\n\n$$\n{a}_{0}={{field-3}}.\n$$\n\nGiven that $F(x)={cos}^{2}⁡(x)$ and $L=4,$ the constant coefficient becomes\n\n$$\n{a}_{0}={{field-4}}\\,\\cdot \\,{{field-5}}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that multiplying the argument of a function by $k\\ne 0$ represents the horizontal stretching of the corresponding graph by a factor of $\\frac{1}{k}.$\n\nNow, let $s=\\frac{\\pi }{L}x.$ Then, since $f(x)$ has a period of $2L,$ the function\n\n$$\ng(s)=f(\\frac{L}{\\pi }s)\n$$\n\nmust have a period of $2L\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{L}=2\\pi .$ \n\nThe Fourier series of $g(s)$ is\n\n$$\ng(s)∼\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(ns)+{b}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(ns),\n$$\n\nwhere:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{0} & =\\frac{1}{\\pi }{\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }g(s)\\,\\text{d}s \\\\ {a}_{n} & =\\frac{1}{\\pi }{\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }g(s)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(ns)\\,\\text{d}s,\\,n\\ge 1 \\\\ {b}_{n} & =\\frac{1}{\\pi }{\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }g(s)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(ns)\\,\\text{d}s,\\,n\\ge 1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $s=\\frac{\\pi }{L}x$ and using the fact that $g(s)=f(\\frac{L}{\\pi }s),$ we get the Fourier series of $f(x):$\n\n$$\nf(x)∼\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi }{L}x)+{b}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi }{L}x)\n$$\n\nTherefore, the constant term of $f(x)$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{0} & =\\frac{1}{\\pi }{\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }g(s)\\,\\text{d}s \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\pi }{\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }f(\\frac{L}{\\pi }s)\\,\\text{d}s \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\pi }{\\int }_{-L}^{L}f(\\frac{L}{\\pi }\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{L}x)\\,\\text{d}(\\frac{\\pi }{L}x) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\pi }\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{L}{\\int }_{-L}^{L}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{L}{\\int }_{-L}^{L}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting $L=4$ and $f(x)={cos}^{2}⁡(x),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{0} & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot {\\int }_{-4}^{4}{cos}^{2}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186317178 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186221444 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "cb301102-1a82-5a81-bb11-b9fc56cd1dc7" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Constant Term For the Fourier Series"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "264561c5-9799-51c9-a009-d1202a71c2b4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315334}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "264561c5-9799-51c9-a009-d1202a71c2b4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315334} :answer-field/id #uuid "79eafde2-60a3-502c-bcb3-a8d0d2d51c6e" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316837}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "e12f9894-53cb-5435-b393-ea7e08594626" :question/math-academy-id "q-341789" :question/problem "$$\nf(x)∼\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(n\\pi x)+{b}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(n\\pi x)\n$$\n\nLet $F(x)=6{x}^{2}+5x+1$ for $x\\in [-1,1).$ The Fourier series of the $2$-periodic extension $f(x)$ of $F(x)$ is shown above. Find the exact value of ${a}_{0}.$\n\n${a}_{0}=$ {{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "For the Fourier series of a $2L$-periodic function, the constant term is given by\n\n$$\n{a}_{0}=\\frac{1}{L}{\\int }_{-L}^{L}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nIn our case, $L=1$ and $f(x)=6{x}^{2}+5x+1$ for $x\\in [-1,1).$ So, substituting into the formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{0} & =\\frac{1}{1}{\\int }_{-1}^{1}(6{x}^{2}+5x+1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[2{x}^{3}+\\frac{5}{2}{x}^{2}+x]}_{-1}^{1} \\\\  & =(2+\\frac{5}{2}+1)-((-2)+\\frac{5}{2}+(-1)) \\\\  & =\\frac{11}{2}-(-\\frac{1}{2}) \\\\  & =6.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186372794 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186221444 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "cb301102-1a82-5a81-bb11-b9fc56cd1dc7" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Constant Term For the Fourier Series"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8c493bcc-7040-54a8-b5d3-429d4cf6c165" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "58" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186372796}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8c493bcc-7040-54a8-b5d3-429d4cf6c165" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "58" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186372796} :answer-field/id #uuid "66bca651-fc67-586c-a6ac-fc1254c6e1f1" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186372795}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "e2e5c8de-82af-59f7-9831-0d0c36257889" :question/math-academy-id "q-341792" :question/problem "$$\nf(x)∼\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi }{6}x)+{b}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi }{6}x)\n$$\n\nLet $F(x)=2{x}^{2}+7x+5$ for $x\\in [-6,6).$ The Fourier series of the $12$-periodic extension $f(x)$ of $F(x)$ is shown above. Find the exact value of ${a}_{0}.$\n\n${a}_{0}=$ {{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "For the Fourier series of a $2L$-periodic function, the constant term is given by\n\n$$\n{a}_{0}=\\frac{1}{L}{\\int }_{-L}^{L}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nIn our case, $L=6$ and $f(x)=2{x}^{2}+7x+5$ for $x\\in [-6,6).$ So, substituting into the formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{0} & =\\frac{1}{6}{\\int }_{-6}^{6}(2{x}^{2}+7x+5)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}{[\\frac{2}{3}{x}^{3}+\\frac{7}{2}{x}^{2}+5x]}_{-6}^{6} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}((\\frac{2}{3}\\cdot {6}^{3}+\\frac{7}{2}\\cdot {6}^{2}+5\\cdot 6)-(\\frac{2}{3}\\cdot (-6)^{3}+\\frac{7}{2}\\cdot (-6)^{2}+5\\cdot (-6))) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}(300-(-48)) \\\\  & =58.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186423256 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186221445 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c3315887-ff5c-5fd7-93bd-a58800e378b8" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Coefficients For the Fourier Series"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "186b12e8-0537-5623-ab6f-d5dfb2e0cdcc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423196}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "186b12e8-0537-5623-ab6f-d5dfb2e0cdcc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423196} :answer-field/id #uuid "ce23bf5e-8b29-5cf7-9b38-cc60d7fad1c9" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423251}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "fc8861f3-8c91-59c6-b70f-78e5364379e8" :question/math-academy-id "q-341817" :question/problem "$$\nf(x)∼\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)+{b}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)\n$$\n\nThe Fourier series of the $2\\pi $-periodic extension $f(x)$ of the function \n\n$$\nF(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}-2, & x\\in [0,\\pi ) \\\\ 3, & x\\in [-\\pi ,0)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nis shown above. Find the exact value of ${a}_{4}.$\n\n${a}_{4}=$ {{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "For the Fourier series of a $2L$-periodic function, the cosine coefficients are given by\n\n$$\n{a}_{n}=\\frac{1}{L}{\\int }_{-L}^{L}f(x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi }{L}x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nIn our case, $L=\\pi .$ Also, $f(x)=-2$ for $x\\in [0,\\pi )$ and $f(x)=3$ for $x\\in [-\\pi ,0).$ So, substituting into the formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{4} & =\\frac{1}{\\pi }{\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }f(x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\pi }{\\int }_{-\\pi }^{0}3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4x)\\,\\text{d}x+\\frac{1}{\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }(-2)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{\\pi }\\cdot \\frac{1}{4}{[\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4x)]}_{-\\pi }^{0}-\\frac{2}{\\pi }\\cdot \\frac{1}{4}{[\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4x)]}_{0}^{\\pi } \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{4\\pi }(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(0)-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(-4\\pi ))-\\frac{1}{2\\pi }(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4\\pi )-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(0)) \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
